     "starter": "class Agent\n- \n+ \n\nclass ToolRegistry\n- \n+ \n\nclass Tool\n- \n+ \n\nclass Budget\n- \n+ \n\nclass Action\n- \n+ \n\nclass Event\n- \n+ \n\nclass RunResult\n- \n+ ",
     "hint": "The agent holds the model, the registry and the limits. A tool holds a name, typed parameters and a function. A budget holds what is used. Action, Event and RunResult are small records.",
     "solution": "class Agent\n- model: any object with next(history)  # the only way we reach the outside\n- registry: ToolRegistry  # tools by name\n- max_steps: int, max_cost: int  # copied into a fresh Budget for each run\n- max_retries: int  # extra attempts after the first, per tool call\n+ run(task) -> RunResult  # req 1: the loop\n+ _execute_tool(action, budget, trace) -> str  # req 2: look up, validate, call\n+ _call_with_retries(tool, args, budget, trace) -> str  # req 3: the retry cap\n+ _within_budget(budget, trace) -> bool  # req 4: checked before every model call\n+ _next_action(history, budget, trace) -> Action  # one charged model call\n\nclass ToolRegistry\n- tools: dict name -> Tool  # lookup by the name the model writes\n+ register(tool) -> void | error  # a duplicate name is refused\n+ get(name) -> Tool | error  # an unknown name is refused\n\nclass Tool\n- name: string  # what the model calls it\n- params: dict name -> type  # the typed arguments\n- fn: function  # the real work; it may raise\n+ validate(args) -> void | error  # req 2: names and exact types\n\nclass Budget\n- max_steps, max_cost: int  # the limits\n- steps, cost: int  # used so far\n+ charge(cost) -> void  # one model call\n+ exhausted() -> 'steps' | 'cost' | None  # req 4\n\nclass Action\n- tool: string | None, args: dict  # a tool call\n- answer: string | None  # or a final answer\n- cost: int  # what this model call cost\n+ is_final() -> bool  # run: stop or keep going\n\nclass Event\n- step: int, kind: string, detail: string  # one line of the trace\n+ line() -> string  # req 5\n\nclass RunResult\n- status: string, answer: string | None, trace: Event[]\n+ ok() -> bool  # did the run finish with an answer",
